Privately Attack Chains =E2=80=94 defensive synthesis

1 NEW ATTACK CHAINS

AC-2026-REPO-PRETRUST-CREDENTIAL =E2=80=94 RECENT / PATCHED-VARIANTS
Aliases: pre-trust repo config exfiltration;
repository-as-executable-config.
Canonical fingerprint: attacker-controlled repository -> developer launches
coding agent in repository -> repository configuration is processed
before/at trust boundary -> code execution or API endpoint redirection ->
ambient agent credential exposed -> potential use of agent/API authority.

Stages:
ENTRY/SOURCE [CONFIRMED, Tier 1]: malicious/untrusted repository containing
agent project configuration.
INITIAL EXECUTION [CONFIRMED, Tier 1]: CVE-2025-59536 allowed Claude Code
<1.0.111 to execute project-controlled code before the startup trust
dialog. CVE-2026-21852 independently exposed project-load ordering that
could redirect ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL before trust and disclose API
credentials; patched in 2.0.65.
PERSISTENCE [UNKNOWN]: neither advisory establishes persistence as
necessary.
SECRET/SESSION/MEMORY ACCESS [CONFIRMED for CVE-2026-21852; UNKNOWN for
CVE-2025-59536]: Anthropic API-key exposure is documented for the former.
PRIVILEGE/AUTHORITY ESCALATION [INFERRED]: possession of an exposed API
credential conveys whatever authority that credential already carries; no
broader privilege escalation is established.
TOOL/CLOUD/CI/SIGNER ACCESS [UNKNOWN].
ACTION/SIGNING/EXFIL [CONFIRMED only to credential exfiltration capability;
downstream use UNKNOWN].
OBSERVED CONSEQUENCE [CONFIRMED]: trust boundary can occur after
security-sensitive project configuration has already been consumed.
CASHOUT/BRIDGE [UNKNOWN / not applicable].

Trust boundary crossed: repository content -> local agent initialization ->
ambient developer credential.
Authority transition: untrusted project configuration influences a process
holding developer/API authority before explicit project trust.
Affected stack: Claude Code historical vulnerable versions; mechanism class
potentially relevant to any coding agent that consumes repository
configuration before trust, but cross-product generalization is INFERRED
only.
Strongest evidence: GitHub-reviewed Anthropic advisory GHSA-4fgq-fpq9-mr3g
/ CVE-2025-59536; OWASP AISVS appendix independently records CVE-2026-21852
and patch version.
Counterevidence/boundary: both named vulnerabilities are patched; this
record is mechanism evidence, not evidence current Claude Code versions
remain vulnerable.
Detection points: coding-agent startup telemetry before trust;
project-config reads; unexpected base-URL changes; outbound API traffic
immediately after opening an untrusted repository.
Containment points: enforce trust before project-controlled configuration
is interpreted; separate ambient credentials from pre-trust initialization;
sandbox pre-trust startup; pin/upgrade patched agent versions.
QP/authority-policy implication: authority should be unavailable until
provenance/trust evaluation completes; project content must not be able to
mutate the authority route used to authenticate the agent.
Safe lab reproduction: disposable repository, local mock API endpoint, fake
token, isolated VM/container, historical vulnerable version only; verify
whether the mock token reaches the mock endpoint before trust. No real
credentials or third-party systems.
Falsifier: a clean current version demonstrably performs no
project-controlled execution/config mutation and emits no
credential-bearing request before trust.
Unresolved: prevalence of equivalent ordering flaws in Cursor/Codex/Gemini
CLI; whether pre-trust repository configuration can reach MCP/session
credentials in current products.

2 MATERIAL CHAIN UPDATES

AC-2026-AGENT-CONFIG-PERSISTENCE / Keyv-ChainDrop cluster =E2=80=94 materia=
lly
strengthened.
Previously: poisoned npm package -> credential harvest -> agent/editor
config implant -> later privileged execution.
Update: multiple independent reports now describe the August Keyv/Cacheable
campaign writing Claude Code and VS Code startup hooks into repositories,
using harvested repository/npm/cloud credentials and propagating into
further packages. This upgrades the edge INITIAL EXECUTION -> REPOSITORY
PERSISTENCE from research-pattern evidence to RECENT incident evidence. The
downstream edge from stolen publishing authority -> poisoned packages is
also CONFIRMED for the campaign family. Claims about compromise of any
particular downstream consumer remain UNKNOWN unless separately evidenced.

3 TOP RECURRING SECOND-ORDER MECHANISMS
A. Trusted package/release authority -> downstream execution.
B. Developer/CI credential harvest -> surviving or newly acquired
publishing/repository authority -> second-order propagation.
C. Repository-controlled agent/editor configuration -> execution that
survives removal of the original poisoned dependency.
D. Agent configuration -> MCP/OAuth route mutation -> delegated SaaS token
exposure.
E. NEW CLUSTER: trust-order inversion =E2=80=94 repository configuration is
consumed before the user trust decision, so the nominal trust prompt is
downstream of the sensitive operation.

4 STAGE/EDGE GRAPHS
PRETRUST: malicious repo [C] -> agent startup [C] -> project config
consumed before trust [C] -> code execution/API redirection [C] -> API
credential exposure [C for CVE-2026-21852] -> downstream authority use [U].
CHAINDROP: poisoned npm [C] -> install execution [C] -> credential harvest
[C] -> repo write authority [C] -> .claude/.vscode persistence [C] -> later
workspace/agent execution [C] -> renewed credential harvest [C] ->
package/repo propagation [C] -> specific downstream privileged action [U].

5 UNKNOWN LINKS WORTH RESOLVING

   1. Whether any current coding agent still processes network-affecting
   repository config before trust.
   2. Whether ChainDrop-compromised repositories caused confirmed later
   cloud/CI/signing actions beyond credential harvesting and package
   propagation.
   3. Whether MCP OAuth tokens can be reached through repository-only
   pre-trust paths without a prior malicious-package execution step.
   4. Whether scanner-discovered current agent harnesses expose analogous
   trust-order inversions.

6 DEFENSIVE CHOKEPOINTS + DETECTION PRIMITIVES
Treat repository-supplied agent configuration as executable content. Gate
all project config behind trust. Remove cloud/package/release credentials
from pre-trust agent environments. File-integrity monitor agent/editor
config and global MCP route configuration. Correlate package lifecycle
execution with subsequent writes to .claude/, .vscode/, MCP config and CI
workflow paths. Detect new publishing/repository actions immediately
following developer credential-access events. Rotate/revoke human, bot,
app, deploy-key, registry and cloud authority together after supply-chain
incidents.

7 SAFE LAB REPRODUCTION QUEUE
P1: historical pre-trust ordering test with fake Anthropic token + local
mock endpoint.
P2: dummy npm package writes inert marker hook into disposable repo;
confirm whether current agent/editor displays/gates execution.
P3: fake MCP OAuth service + dummy bearer token; measure whether
route/config changes are visible and attributable.
P4: disposable Git repository with fake package-publish token; model
credential rotation while deliberately leaving one dummy bot credential to
test residual-authority detection.

8 CROSS-CASE CLUSTERS
CL-TRUST-ORDER-INVERSION: CVE-2025-59536 + CVE-2026-21852. First seen 2025;
latest public synthesis 2026-09; status RECENT/PATCHED-VARIANTS.
CL-AGENT-CONFIG-PERSISTENCE: Keyv/ChainDrop + earlier SAP/Mini-Shai-Hulud
reporting. Status ACTIVE/RECENT mechanism.
CL-DELEGATED-AUTHORITY-HIJACK: MCP OAuth route hijack research + agent
global configuration mutation. Status LAB_ONLY/RECENT research; real
downstream malicious SaaS actions UNKNOWN.
CL-RELEASE-AUTHORITY-CASCADE: Trivy/Red Hat/npm cases from prior state.
Status RECENT.

